          %h2#in_string_theory In string theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                In
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-monopole"} KK-monopole
              %p
                In
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D7-brane"} D7-brane
          %h2#references References
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+classification"} ADE classification
            of 4d ALE-spaces is due to
          %ul
            %li#Kronheimer89
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Kronheimer"}> Peter Kronheimer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The construction of ALE spaces as hyper-Kähler quotients
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jdg/1214443066"} Euclid
          %p In
          %ul
            %li#IntriligatorSeiberg96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ken+Intriligator"}> Ken Intriligator
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathan+Seiberg"} Nathan Seiberg
              %em Mirror Symmetry in Three Dimensional Gauge Theories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9607207"}> arXiv:hep-th/9607207
              )
          %p
            this result is interpreted physically as describing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacua"} vacua
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theories"} gauge theories
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spontaneously+broken+symmetry"} spontaneously broken symmetry
            (“Higgs branches”). See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3d+mirror+symmetry"} 3d mirror symmetry
            for more on this.
          %p
            For application in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-monopole"} KK-monopole
            and see
          %ul
            %li#JohnsonMyers96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+Johnson"}> Clifford Johnson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Myers"} Robert Myers
              = succeed "," do
                %em Aspects of Type IIB Theory on ALE Spaces
              = succeed ")" do
